From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:08:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] main: end a helper with the netifd that started it

A protocol helper that netifd_start_process() starts (udhcpc, odhcp6c,
pppd and the protocol scripts) stays alive when netifd dies. procd
starts netifd again, which starts the helpers again, so each crash left
a second udhcpc and odhcp6c on the interface.

Set PR_SET_PDEATHSIG to SIGTERM in the child, and end the child at once
where netifd died before that. Restore the default SIGTERM action first,
since the child runs the handler of netifd until execve(). The setting
holds across setsid() and across execve() of a program without
set-user-ID bits or file capabilities, so it reaches every helper
netifd runs in the foreground. udhcpc runs with -f, odhcp6c without -d
and pppd with nodetach. It does not reach a process that a helper
forks, such as the scripts a DHCP client calls, or a helper that
daemonises itself. The hotplug scripts of interface-event.c and the
processes of ucode.c start through their own fork() and are not
changed.

A DHCP client that ends this way releases its lease, since dhcp.sh runs
udhcpc with -R and dhcpv6.sh runs odhcp6c without -k unless norelease
is set.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
(cherry picked from commit 8da363f546f579bfc039828e0bc4d061f878bcb0)
---
 main.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index f114b4a..2c51ab1 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -19,6 +19,8 @@
 #include <stdarg.h>
 #include <syslog.h>
 #include <errno.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#include <sys/prctl.h>
 
 #include "netifd.h"
 #include "ubus.h"
@@ -208,6 +210,7 @@ netifd_add_process(struct netifd_process *proc, int fd, int pid)
 int
 netifd_start_process(const char **argv, char **env, struct netifd_process *proc)
 {
+	pid_t parent = getpid();
 	int pfds[2];
 	int pid;
 
@@ -222,6 +225,15 @@ netifd_start_process(const char **argv, char **env, struct netifd_process *proc)
 	if (!pid) {
 		int i;
 
+		/*
+		 * The netifd that procd starts after a crash runs the protocol
+		 * helpers again, so a helper of the dead one must end with it.
+		 */
+		signal(SIGTERM, SIG_DFL);
+		prctl(PR_SET_PDEATHSIG, SIGTERM);
+		if (getppid() != parent)
+			_exit(127);
+
 		if (env) {
 			while (*env) {
 				putenv(*env);
